   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Chat to Preview Layout\n\nA two-up split where the chat panel shrinks and the preview panel expands, to show an agent building something. Both panels hold generic placeholder content. On a tall frame the split stacks vertically (chat on top).\n\nCategory: layout. Length: 4 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- Showing an AI agent at work: the conversation starts as the subject, then yields the frame to what it produced.\n- You need a two-column split whose ratio animates, with no cut.\n\nAvoid when:\n- Both columns should stay the same size: use a plain flex row.\n- The change between the two states is a cut rather than a squeeze: use a transition.\n\nVariables:\n- start_chat_ratio (number, 0.1-0.9): Start chat ratio, default 0.5\n- end_chat_ratio (number, 0.05-0.9): End chat ratio, default 0.25\n- chat_title (string): Chat label, default \"Chat\"\n- messages (string): Messages, default \"> Build me a landing page\\nSure, what should it feature?\\n> Hero, pricing, footer.\\nOn it. Generating now...\"\n- headline (string): Preview headline, default \"Ship faster.\"\n- subline (string): Preview text, default \"The fastest way to launch your idea.\"\n- cta (string): Preview button, default \"Get started\"\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
